<title>ITALY: Italy November producer prices rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Italy November producer prices rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office ISTAT gave the following Italian producer price data for November.</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES	   Nov 96    Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p>    Year/year change	  +0.6 pct  +0.4 pct     +7.2 pct</p>
<p>    Month/month change	+0.2 pct  +0.2 pct	0.0 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990=100)    124.6     124.4	  123.9</p>
<p>Istat gave the following general breakdown:</p>
<p>				  Mo/Mo change (%)    Yr/Yr change (%)</p>
<p>    Consumer goods		   0.0		    +1.5</p>
<p>    Investment goods		 0.0		    +2.9</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods	    +0.3		    -0.3</p>
<p>It gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown:</p>
<p>    Sector			    mo/mo (%)	     yr/yr (%)</p>
<p>    Energy products		 +1.5		   +6.1</p>
<p>    Minerals and metals	    0.0		   -9.3</p>
<p>    Non-metal minerals	     0.0		   +0.7</p>
<p>    Pharamceutical/chemicals    -0.4		   -2.9</p>
<p>    Metal works		     -0.1		   +1.9</p>
<p>    Cars and parts		   0.0		   +4.5</p>
<p>    Food, drink and tobacco	0.0		   +0.5</p>
<p>    Clothing, leather goods	0.0		   +0.5</p>
<p>    Other goods		     +0.1		   -1.5</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
